1", "year": 2016, "make": "Audi", "model": "A3", "trim": "2.0T Premium", "price": 12500, "mileage": 84000, "location": "Berwyn, PA", "distanceMi": 4, "url": "https://www.autotrader.com/cars-for-sale/vehicledetails.xhtml?listingId=780193901", "dealer": null, "dealRating": null, "cleanTitle": null, "noAccidents": true, "transmission": null, "imageUrl": "https://images2.autotrader.com/hn/c/45f995f2bd1e4e8d8d4795af0ad3532e.jpg", "source": "autotrader"}]}, "truecar": {"totalFound": 0, "url": "", "listings": []}, "top10": {"introHtml": "<p>Ranked by condition over miles — cars with exceptionally low annual mileage or strong value-to-condition ratio. All are 4-seat convertibles passing the clean-title/no-accidents filters where verified. Prices as of 2026-10-16.</p>", "picks": [{"year": 2012, "make": "Fiat", "model": "500", "imageUrl": "https://platform.cstatic-images.com/in/v2/915dc978-cb40-5160-94a4-afaa35adacb8/c420cd74-1dd7-456f-8d32-dce23b687648/4N-ie81lOSRq4rGZrGnhHCilijs.jpg", "whyGood": "Only 16,848 miles on a 2012—essentially fresh. The 500C's retractable soft top lets you open up in 2 seconds. Under 1,200 miles/year means this car was barely driven; seals and mechanicals are almost certainly in excellent shape.", "whatToVerify": "Have a pre-purchase inspection check for dry-rot on weatherstripping and soft-top frame. Fiat 500s can have electrical gremlins; test all windows, radio, and the top cycle completely. Check for any coolant or oil seepage.", "bottomLine": "A near-mint convertible under $14K. If the inspection is clean, this is the best-preserved car in the entire search."}, {"year": 2007, "make": "BMW", "model": "328", "imageUrl": "https://platform.cstatic-images.com/in/v2/84f99b5a-f558-5eec-a1f1-3c0a5bf0dad5/83cb0200-6ad9-4e36-9483-590b61fc3260/BEkzJCCe0x-Xp5clESordw27DQU.jpg", "whyGood": "Only 34,412 miles on a 2007 E93 BMW—barely 1,800 miles/year average. The E93 3-Series convertible is widely regarded as one of the best-balanced, most reliable BMW convertibles ever built. A 34K-mile example is exceptional.", "whatToVerify": "At this mileage, timing chain stretch is less of a concern but check anyway. Inspect the power-folding hardtop mechanism—all stages, open and close, multiple times. Check HVAC, all windows, and look for any structural rust on the subframe.", "bottomLine": "Low-mile E93 at $14,485 is a genuine deal—this car would cost nearly double with fresh dealer reconditioning."}, {"year": 2008, "make": "BMW", "model": "135i", "imageUrl": "https://images2.autotrader.com/hn/c/48e6e5f8e26f4c9ab27d9520494927ca.jpg", "whyGood": "48,000 miles on an 18-year-old BMW is remarkably low. The 135i's turbocharged N54 inline-six makes 300hp in a lightweight convertible body—easily one of the most fun cars in this search. At $11,995, you're buying a sports car for grocery-run money.", "whatToVerify": "N54 engine: check for high-pressure fuel pump issues, wastegate rattle, and injector seals. Convertible top motor can be pricey; cycle it 3-4 times. No-accident report not confirmed—check Carfax.", "bottomLine": "Performance bargain of the search. The 135i punches far above its price; budget an extra $500 for a thorough independent inspection."}, {"year": 2005, "make": "Jaguar", "model": "XK8", "imageUrl": "https://platform.cstatic-images.com/in/v2/a733be78-f490-4868-adbe-201a3d056e0c/2a597d81-324b-4fc6-9886-1436a47ae8f9/Uw_rKHIXYfis06fXa6LAWVVZJH0.jpg", "whyGood": "The XK8 is a gorgeous 2+2 grand tourer with a silky 4.2L V8. At 51,549 miles for $13,950, you're getting a car that would have cost $80K new. Great Deal badge confirms the price is solid. Low miles suggest careful prior ownership.", "whatToVerify": "Jaguar XK8: inspect carefully for rear subframe corrosion (known issue), timing chain tensioner health, and AJ-V8 coolant leaks. Check all four air suspension components if equipped. Convertible top hydraulics are reliable but test all latches.", "bottomLine": "A stunning grand tourer at a fraction of original MSRP. Budget for Jaguar maintenance costs—this is a splurge buy, not a cheap buy."}, {"year": 1995, "make": "Jaguar", "model": "XJS", "imageUrl": "https://platform.cstatic-images.com/in/v2/2a9ff44c-1d8c-572a-b85a-e2c017e560ce/eec71dc7-9fe7-4cbe-86f1-4f071ac06ac8/5WgTTGYREAi4bO4kfEPlo0Ncpmw.jpg", "whyGood": "46,000 miles on a 1995 XJS—the last and best year of this model. Only 1,484 miles/year average is almost unbelievably low. The XJS 2+2 has proper rear seats and one of the most beautiful bodies in automotive history. At $9,399, this is a collector-grade car at a daily-driver price.", "whatToVerify": "Pre-purchase inspection is non-negotiable on a 30-year-old British car. Check for: coolant system integrity, wiring loom condition (notorious on XJS), convertible top hydraulics, and rust underneath. Find an independent Jaguar specialist.", "bottomLine": "A genuine collector car with impeccable mileage. The right XJS bought right is a joy; the wrong one is a money pit—inspect thoroughly."}, {"year": 2003, "make": "BMW", "model": "330", "imageUrl": "https://platform.cstatic-images.com/in/v2/915dc978-cb40-5160-94a4-afaa35adacb8/85261c6d-9dc8-4f72-b1a8-9244ecccaf79/iDrG-hqKtpND5Nw-jIG8TFqzBO4.jpg", "whyGood": "64,358 miles on the beloved E46 330Ci—widely considered the peak of BMW driving dynamics. Clean title, no accidents (Cars.com verified). The E46 convertible has real rear seats, excellent handling, and strong parts support. At $9,495, it's one of the best value-performance buys in this search.", "whatToVerify": "E46 330Ci: check cooling system (water pump, thermostat, expansion tank are common failures), VANOS system, and rear subframe reinforcement plates (cracks are fixable but important). Convertible top: test all stages including glass rear window defogging.", "bottomLine": "The enthusiast's pick under $10K. Properly maintained E46 convertibles are among the most rewarding sports cars you can own at any price."}, {"year": 2013, "make": "Infiniti", "model": "G37", "imageUrl": "https://platform.cstatic-images.com/in/v2/c04447ce-c7d6-5b50-ab72-ee5ab9e22495/0b874690-9551-4d99-80c5-1dbaef9155a7/_-JgjyfWJX49WmwFZTNGlFn03pI.jpg", "whyGood": "The G37 Convertible pairs a 330hp V6 with a proper 4-seat convertible body. Great Deal badge at Faulkner INFINITI (a dealer!) means they've vetted it. 91,309 miles is solid for a 2013. Clean title, no accidents confirmed.", "whatToVerify": "G37 Convertibles are known to be reliable; check for VQ37VHR engine oil leaks (common), inspect the power convertible top for full operation, and verify the tonneau cover closes completely. Check rear seat headroom—it's tight.", "bottomLine": "Modern, reliable, fast—the G37 Convertible is the practical performance pick. $13,489 at a dealer with Great Deal rating is hard to argue with."}, {"year": 2012, "make": "Audi", "model": "A5", "imageUrl": "https://platform.cstatic-images.com/in/v2/p2p/16b786f6-0c39-436c-95a7-05465908b11d/01d78260-a9ec-422a-8a85-d830ecdabb8f", "whyGood": "The Audi A5 Cabriolet is a stunning 2+2 with a premium soft top. 80,410 miles at $8,995 puts you in a car with Audi's smooth 2.0T engine and refined interior for under $9K. Clean title, no accidents confirmed.", "whatToVerify": "2.0T TFSI: check for carbon buildup on intake valves (common on direct-injection engines), timing chain tensioner, and any DSG/S-Tronic service history. Soft top: check for tears, water leaks at the pillars, and confirm the rear window defogging works.", "bottomLine": "Premium German convertible under $9K with documented clean history—excellent value if the mechanicals are sound."}, {"year": 2010, "make": "Audi", "model": "S5", "imageUrl": "https://static.cargurus.com/images/forsale/2026/09/26/05/17/2010_audi_s5-pic-4518652174160034455-1024x768.jpeg", "whyGood": "The S5 Cabriolet packs a supercharged 3.0T V6 making 333hp—this is the performance Audi cabriolet. Quattro AWD means year-round usability. Good Deal rating at $10,489 with 92,034 miles. Both Cars.com and AutoTrader show this car, confirming the listing.", "whatToVerify": "3.0T supercharger: check for oil leaks around the snout seal and intercooler connections. Quattro drivetrain: listen for any rear differential or center diff noise. Convertible top: test the full cycle. Check for typical Audi electronic niggle codes.", "bottomLine": "The best-performing car in this search for the money. Four seats, four seasons, 333hp—the S5 Cabriolet is a genuine bargain at this price."}, {"year": 2002, "make": "Mitsubishi", "model": "Eclipse", "imageUrl": "https://platform.cstatic-images.com/in/v2/73ea6201-0793-408c-8eb2-98f1ae413f64/b6ef0ac8-37a8-4fa1-924f-a2178f48e5e9/rMftMuioeKePyLC8sIHVxGFKCcI.jpg", "whyGood": "71,811 miles on the Eclipse Spyder GT—the V6-powered version with real rear seats. Clean title, no accidents. At $8,895, this is the most affordable V6 sporty convertible in the search with documented clean history. Eclipse Spyder GTs are increasingly collectable.", "whatToVerify": "3G Eclipse GT: check for timing belt service (critical—interference engine), inspect the convertible top frame for cracks or bent sections, and verify the rear hatch seal doesn't leak. Look for any frame flex at the doorsill.", "bottomLine": "Budget pick with sporty credentials. At $8,895 with verified no-accident history, it's a solid starter convertible or weekend car."}]}, "manual10": {"totalFound": 0, "introHtml": "<p>No confirmed manual-transmission convertibles were found in today's search. Transmission data was not available in listing cards for most vehicles. Check individual listings on Cars.com or AutoTrader for transmission filter options.</p>", "picks": []}, "mustangs": {"totalFound": 2, "introHtml": "<p>Ford Mustang convertibles 2005 and newer, $7K–$15K, within 35 miles of ZIP 19063. 2 found today.</p>", "picks": [{"year": 2014, "make": "Ford", "model": "Mustang", "imageUrl": "https://images2.autotrader.com/hn/c/78156f1c7b50469b9b0490551d6b1044.jpg", "whyGood": "121,000 miles but priced accordingly at $9,442. The 2014 Mustang Convertible uses the proven 3.7L V6 (305hp) or 5.0 V8—confirm which. No accidents reported. This generation has excellent parts support and a strong enthusiast community.", "whatToVerify": "Verify engine spec (V6 vs V8 dramatically changes maintenance costs). Check for rear axle bearing wear (common on high-mile Mustangs), convertible top mechanical operation, and any structural flex issues. At 121K, ask about recent service.", "bottomLine": "Affordable modern Mustang convertible. Get the Carfax and confirm the drivetrain spec before committing."}, {"year": 2020, "make": "Ford", "model": "Mustang", "imageUrl": "https://images2.autotrader.com/hn/c/78156f1c7b50469b9b0490551d6b1044.jpg", "whyGood": "The newest car in the Mustang section at $9,994—sixth-gen Mustang with modern infotainment, driver aids, and significantly improved suspension. Premium trim means upgraded interior and likely the 2.3L EcoBoost or 5.0 V8. 132K miles at this price is the tradeoff.", "whatToVerify": "Verify engine (EcoBoost vs GT). At 132K, check EcoBoost turbo for oil leaks and carbon buildup. Confirm the 10-speed auto (if equipped) has been serviced. Modern convertible top: test all electronic latches and the rear window at all temperatures.", "bottomLine": "Most modern Mustang at the lowest price in search. High miles are the concern; the updated platform justifies them if maintenance history is solid."}]}}